### call_hierarchy_test_errors.md — 5/6 passed

| Test | Result | Actual |
|------|--------|--------|
| testInvalidDirection | **PASS** | Error: `"direction must be 'callers' or 'callees'"` |
| testMissingDirection | **PASS** | Error: `"Missing required parameter: direction"` |
| testNonExistentFile | **PASS** | Error: `"No element found at position .../nonexistent.rb:1:5"` |
| testPositionOutsideMethod | **FAIL** | See details below |
| testSymbolBasedLookup | **FAIL (expected)** | Error: `"Ruby symbol resolution is not yet implemented"` |
| testEmptyFile | **PASS** | Error: `"No element found at position .../empty.rb:1:1"` |

**testPositionOutsideMethod diagnosis**: The test points at line 1, column 1
(`class Calculator`) which is outside any method. The tool returns the same
error message as when a position IS inside a valid method:
`"No method/function found at position"`. The two scenarios are
indistinguishable from the error alone. The test stated expectation was an
error containing `"No method/function found"` — which matches — but the test
also intended to verify this is distinguishable from a valid-position query,
which it is not.

**testSymbolBasedLookup diagnosis**: This is a known stub. The tool validates
the symbol format (`Greeter#hello`) but returns `"Ruby symbol resolution is not
yet implemented"`. This is documented/expected behavior per the test
instructions.

